{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "or-duplicate-merge-2026-09-15",
    "name": "OpenRegister Duplicate Merge And Dismissed Pairs",
    "description": "The merge choice, the dismissed pair and the soft uniqueness alert, asserted where CI can see them.\n\nWHAT IT ASSERTS, each paired with its control:\n  * a nominated field warns on save and the save still succeeds, because the hint is an alert and not a constraint\n  * a unique-hint naming a property the schema does not declare is refused with 422 at schema save\n  * the scorer offers a pair BEFORE it is dismissed (the control) and stops offering it after\n  * a dismissal names the actor, the reason, the moment and a fingerprint\n  * the merge preview offers both values and a proposal per property\n  * a decision map that omits a property the preview offered is refused with 422, and the control after it shows nothing was written\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT ASSERT. The refusal on an unreadable property needs a second user in a group this collection cannot create, and fingerprint expiry needs both sides controlled exactly; both are covered by unit tests named in the PR body.\n\nSELF-CLEANING. It creates its own register, schema and objects and removes all of them.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
